Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["KPPS Quartic 2-Matrix Models", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"1c3c47d3-e5f3-4c28-8a05-eccde03ca9c8"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The Action", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"89f6bb3c-3c5c-4f91-a92e-fe941cc10935"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["S", "N"], "=", 
    RowBox[{"N", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        FractionBox["1", "2"], " ", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          SuperscriptBox[
           SubscriptBox["M", "0"], "2"], "+", 
          SuperscriptBox[
           SubscriptBox["M", "1"], "2"]}], ")"}]}], "+", 
       RowBox[{
        FractionBox[
         SubscriptBox["g", "1"], "4"], " ", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          SuperscriptBox[
           SubscriptBox["M", "0"], "4"], "+", 
          SuperscriptBox[
           SubscriptBox["M", "1"], "4"]}], ")"}]}], "+", 
       RowBox[{
        FractionBox[
         SubscriptBox["g", "2"], "2"], " ", 
        SubscriptBox["M", "0"], " ", 
        SubscriptBox["M", "1"], " ", 
        SubscriptBox["M", "0"], " ", 
        SubscriptBox["M", "1"]}], "+", 
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["g", "3"], " ", 
        SuperscriptBox[
         SubscriptBox["M", "0"], "2"], " ", 
        SuperscriptBox[
         SubscriptBox["M", "1"], "2"]}]}], "]"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"b8280360-9553-48a4-b321-cae3853de756"],
 ".\n\n",
 "The resolvent is taken over ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["M", "0"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "63006a2f-e890-42bf-a8c3-e6224b562347"],
 ", so the cyclic derivative of the action is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["M", "0"], "+", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["g", "1"], " ", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      SubscriptBox["M", "0"], "3"]}], "+", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["g", "2"], " ", 
     SubscriptBox["M", "1"], " ", 
     SubscriptBox["M", "0"], " ", 
     SubscriptBox["M", "1"]}], "+", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["g", "3"], " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["M", "0"], " ", 
        SuperscriptBox[
         SubscriptBox["M", "1"], "2"]}], "+", 
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox[
         SubscriptBox["M", "1"], "2"], " ", 
        SubscriptBox["M", "0"]}]}], ")"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"bcc99217-c2e7-45f1-9710-4c8a9989d117"],
 ". The second derivative follows by exchanging the two matrices. The ordered \
products distinguish the two mixed quartic interactions.\n\n",
 "The signs label ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    SubscriptBox["g", "1"], ",", 
    SubscriptBox["g", "2"], ",", 
    SubscriptBox["g", "3"], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"f66bf03f-6b94-41bd-9cdd-ad4c1401fcbd"],
 " in that order: ppp = (g,g,g), pmp = (g,-g,g), mpp = (-g,g,g), and ppm = \
(g,g,-g). The coupling g and spectral parameter z remain symbolic.\n\n",
 "Correlator labels are identified under cyclic rotation, reversal and \
exchange of the matrices. Independent sign changes of either matrix set \
correlators with an odd number of either label to zero; auxiliary resolvents \
with an odd number of explicit 1 labels also vanish."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"184385f3-1126-4557-921e-2e70876056fa"]
}, Closed]],

